  "limits": [
    "Box impulses, free-flight drag/gravity and angular decisions run at 30 Hz. Visual rotation uses floating-point Three.js matrices and contacts use the fork mesh query, not the original quantized matrix/collision engine.",
    "Random targets use an independent deterministic per-prop stream, not the original global RNG. Sound uses an existing local effect.",
    "Player-to-prop contact is sampled after each 60 Hz player step. The source invokes it during its 30 Hz state pipeline before static collision; full state-order parity is not claimed.",
    "The dedicated upper case starts once on the supported raised platform. It proves both stack contacts and rollout, not a complete approach to the platform. Preliminary flat/late-ollie approaches hit an existing raised edge even with props disabled; they are not counted as successful routes.",
    "A soft level reset hides already-hit props; a hard restart restores all original placements. Below-kill-plane cleanup is a fork lifecycle policy.",
    "The asset records are retained original Mall data in THPS2 retail; not byte-verified against a 1999 THPS1 disc."
  ],
  "inputContract": "Each gameplay case starts at rest once on supported floor, then uses ordinary controller input. Contact micro-fixtures use explicit standalone prop setups; they are not claimed as level traversal."
